  "name": "Work and Pensions Committee",
  "parent_committee_id": null,
  "purpose": "<p>The Work and Pensions Committee looks into the policies and spending of the Department for Work and Pensions, including benefits for people in and out of work, state pensions and how private pensions are regulated. It also scrutinises DWP’s public bodies and other regulators.</p>\r\n<p>Follow us on social media:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/hoccommittees.parliament.uk\">Bluesky</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ukcommonscommittees\">Instagram</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61579513151155\">Facebook</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/house-of-commons-committees/\">LinkedIn</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/user/UKCommonsCommittees/\">Reddit</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://x.com/HoCcommitteesUK\">X</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLj3mInRJqIekxA--aDW780T_TUCwjea4M\">YouTube</a>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/email/committeecorridor\">Subscribe to the Committee Corridor newsletter</a> for a weekly round-up of news, inquiry updates and reports from House of Commons committees.</p>",
